    [Performance][GLM] Reuse convolution output buffers and remove redundant KDA clears (#19408)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Reuse a fixed convolution output buffer across layers in each GLM-5.3
    Flash attention group, clearing it once during metadata preparation.
    Preserve zero decode padding and remove redundant KDA output pre-clears.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No API or configuration changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Existing dispatch/metadata tests, lint and mypy passed in
    [CI](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/39715018881);
    CPU tests passed with vLLM main and v0.31.0.
    - Selected GDN NPU regressions are running; GLM shared-buffer hardware
    validation is pending.
    
    Accuracy results supplied for the preceding output-clear removal
    revision:
    
    | Dataset | PR accuracy | Baseline accuracy |
    | --- | --- | --- |
    | GPQA-Diamond | 175/198 (88.38%) | 175/198 (88.38%) |
    | AIME26 | 29/30 (96.67%) | 29/30 (96.67%) |
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: ZYang6263 <50876451+ZYang6263@users.noreply.github.com>

